  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Pulse Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a pulse survey?\", \"a\": \"A pulse survey asks the same people a few fixed questions on a set cycle, often every week or two. Each round takes a couple of minutes, and comparing rounds shows whether a team's answers are climbing or sliding. The US Census Bureau also runs a Household Pulse Survey, started in April 2020.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you build an employee pulse survey?\", \"a\": \"Describe to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> who answers and how often. It drafts the questions and a results view split by team, and it is free to start. Send round one to a single team as a trial before the rest of the company sees it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide an example of a pulse survey question?\", \"a\": \"\\\"My workload is manageable this week,\\\" rated on a 1-5 agreement scale, is a typical one. It covers one thing and still makes sense next round. Good pulse survey questions describe a present condition the team can change, not a general feeling about the company.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free pulse survey template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent writes a pulse survey template from a few lines of description, and you can start for free. Ask for a handful of employee pulse survey questions and say who hears about a falling score. Settle the wording before round one goes out. Changing it later breaks the trend line.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a college pulse survey real?\", \"a\": \"Yes. College Pulse is an online survey and analytics company that studies US undergraduates through its own student panel. It has no connection to the pulse surveys an employer sends its staff, which share only the name.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should you run employee pulse surveys?\", \"a\": \"Weekly or every other week suits a set of about five statements, and a monthly round can carry more. Match the cadence to how fast you can act on what comes back. If a team needs two weeks to discuss results, a weekly round outruns it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is another name for a pulse survey?\", \"a\": \"Pulse check is the name you hear most, and some teams say check-in survey or micro-survey. All three mean the same format: the same handful of questions repeated on a schedule and read as a trend, not as one result. The format works with customers too, as a two-question monthly check beside a quarterly customer satisfaction survey.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are pulse surveys anonymous?\", \"a\": \"Some are, and others are confidential, which is a different promise. A confidential pulse knows who answered and can send reminders, but it hides any group below a minimum number of answers. An anonymous pulse stores no identity at all, which rules out reminders and team splits.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should employee pulse survey software do?\", \"a\": \"It should send each round on schedule and nudge only those still missing. It should also hide small groups and chart each team against its own history. Ask where the data lives, and whether you can export it if you change tools later. On Emergent the answers land in a database you own, and no cap limits how many come in.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does an employee engagement pulse survey differ from an annual one?\", \"a\": \"An annual <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-engagement-survey'>employee engagement survey</a> asks dozens of items once a year to find what drives commitment. An employee engagement pulse survey repeats a handful of those core items between annual rounds. It shows whether the actions managers took are moving the score.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
